.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-roster-import-token - Put an API token minted outside pveforge into the roster, once PVE proves its grants


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge roster import-token <target-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Import an API token minted outside pveforge into the roster.

.PP
The secret is read from stdin, which must NOT be a terminal: pipe it from
wherever the token was minted. There is no flag or environment variable for
it. The roster passphrase therefore cannot be prompted for either: set
PVEFORGE_ROSTER_PASSPHRASE.

.PP
Before anything is written, PVE is asked, as the token, what it can do, and
that must be exactly the --grant scopes (the validation bootstrap runs). A
token that fails is not written, and nothing on PVE is ever touched: an import
creates nothing there, so it never revokes anything.

.PP
A target that already holds a DIFFERENT token is refused unless --replace is
given; the replaced token is not revoked and stays live on PVE. Importing the
token the target already holds is a no-op (already_held).

.PP
An imported target holds a token but no SSH key, so a later plain
"pveforge bootstrap" of it is refused: pass --no-ssh-key to keep it keyless.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--api-port\fP=0
	the target's API port (default 8006)

.PP
\fB--grant\fP=[]
	a scope the token must hold, PATH:ROLE[:PRIVS[:PROPAGATE]] (repeatable, at least one; the token must hold exactly these)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for import-token

.PP
\fB--host\fP=""
	the target's API host (defaults to the roster's, required for a new target)

.PP
\fB--insecure-tls\fP[=false]
	skip TLS verification for a new target's API

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB--node\fP=""
	the target's node name (defaults to the roster's, required for a new target)

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"

.PP
\fB--replace\fP[=false]
	replace a different token the target already holds (the old token is not revoked)

.PP
\fB--token-id\fP=""
	the full token id, <user>@<realm>!<token name> (required)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-roster(1)\fP
